# Static routes

`getPublication()` is the common eligible view for route identity, metadata,
writing, showcase and export. `src/pages/[...path].astro` derives ordinary reader
routes from it; `index.astro` and `404.astro` provide home and genuine error documents.
Do not maintain an independent route/sitemap/navigation metadata list.

New reviewed Markdown/MDX originals use explicit stable permalinks and the shared
collection. They need no Vite HTML shell or mount entry. Follow
`docs/operations/authoring.md` for the full promotion contract. Preserve all existing
work, experience and note URLs and the complete reviewed article titles.

`WorkspaceShell.astro` owns document metadata, apex canonicals, robots/Open Graph,
guarded pre-paint theme bootstrap, accessible navigation and a single Firebase
bootstrap. Reader prose and links exist before JavaScript; React is for actual
interactive controls. There is no SPA router or catch-all rewrite.

The build-only `/publication-manifest.json` is excluded from the public artifact.
The 404 is useful and non-indexable, absent from the sitemap. Contents links target
real headings; mobile has native inline contents and normal navigation disclosure.
Preserve semantic landmarks, focus visibility, reduced motion and ordinary links.
